cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use SkillLift in your research, please cite it using the metadata below."
title: "SkillLift"
type: software
license: MIT
abstract: "SkillLift is an evaluation framework for self-evolving agent skills. It runs the SkillLift portfolio coordinator (Mode A verifier-guided refinement, Mode B oracle-aligned rubric revision) and reproduction baselines against the WildClawBench, tau2-bench, and SkillsBench benchmarks under matched context and token budgets."
repository-code: "https://github.com/WalteR-MittY-pro/SkillLift"
url: "https://github.com/WalteR-MittY-pro/SkillLift"
keywords:
  - AI agents
  - agent skills
  - self-evolving skills
  - benchmark evaluation
  - LLM agents
authors:
